  "verbalization": "Nodulisporic Acid is shown to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through multiple pathways, with varying levels of confidence. The first pathway links Nodulisporic Acid to Thrombopoietin, which is then identified as a target of a complex molecule that ultimately targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The second pathway connects Nodulisporic Acid to DNA polymerase iota, which is also targeted by another complex molecule that ultimately targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The third pathway similarly links Nodulisporic Acid to Thrombopoietin, which is then targeted by a complex molecule that ultimately targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These findings suggest that Nodulisporic Acid may act as a modulator of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through different molecular mechanisms, possibly by influencing the activity or expression of downstream targets. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, indicating a potential role for Nodulisporic Acid in regulating the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
